	// B.Children contains [X, C, C] (unsorted, duplicate C that Parents
	// disagree with? no—) Set up C already depends on B but B lists C twice,
	// plus a bogus order. Re-register C dropping B then... simpler: C is a
	// root; B.Children wrongly? Legality: names correspond and references
	// valid. If B lists C twice while C.Parents has B, that's "legal" per
	// task (duplicates allowed in hand-built graph).
